Tile 3.5: CPU I/O wait by app

Average over the selected time range, one row per affected host, with Open with → Hosts support.

timeseries io = avg(dt.host.cpu.iowait), by:{dt.entity.host}
| fieldsAdd iowaitPct = round(arrayAvg(io), decimals:1)
| filter iowaitPct >= 20
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.host | fields id, hostName = entity.name, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: id, prefix: "h."
| expand tag = h.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| fieldsAdd risk = if(iowaitPct >= 40, "🔴 Critical", else: "🟠 Warning")
| fieldsAdd appHost = concat(apmid, " | ", h.hostName)
| fields risk, appHost, iowaitPct, dt.entity.host
| sort iowaitPct desc

Visual: Table. Tile timeframe: Last 2 hours.
Thresholds: 20% = Warning, 40% = Critical. These are starting values to adjust once you see real data.
cpu.iowait is mainly reported by Linux and AIX hosts (~400 series), so Windows hosts won't appear.
If you get no records, temporarily change >= 20 to >= 1 to check that the query works.
Tile 3.6: Recent reboots (uptime under 24h)

This is the query from my earlier message, unchanged:

timeseries up = avg(dt.host.uptime), by:{dt.entity.host}, from:-30m
| fieldsAdd uptimeSec = arrayLast(arrayRemoveNulls(up))
| filter isNotNull(uptimeSec) and uptimeSec < 86400
| fieldsAdd uptimeHrs = round(uptimeSec / 3600, decimals:1)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.host | fields id, hostName = entity.name, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: id, prefix: "h."
| expand tag = h.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| fieldsAdd appHost = concat(apmid, " | ", h.hostName)
| fields appHost, uptimeHrs, dt.entity.host
| sort uptimeHrs asc


